WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:07.120
Hi, Mystery Recapped here. Today I am going&nbsp;
to explain a South Korean comedy film called&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:11.280
“Timer.” Spoilers ahead!&nbsp;
Watch out and take care!
&nbsp;

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:20.960
In the near future, a device is developed&nbsp;
which allows one to see the exact time they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:26.080
will meet their soulmate. It is called the next&nbsp;
revolutionary step in digital matchmaking by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:32.400
many. A facility called the “Timer” offers such&nbsp;
service to common people. They insert a chip on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:37.200
your wrist that counts down to the day you meet&nbsp;
your soulmate. When two soulmates come in close&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:42.560
proximity, the timer goes off, letting them know&nbsp;
that they have met each other. However, the timer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:48.000
won’t start until both the people have gotten&nbsp;
the chip embedded in their wrists. Oona is a Los&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:53.600
Angeles orthodontist who has an unblinking timer,&nbsp;
meaning that her soulmate isn’t equipped with one.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:58.000
She has come to the Timer office with her&nbsp;
recent boyfriend to find out if he is really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:03.280
the one. The worker named Matchmaker Patty is&nbsp;
good friends with Oona because she is one of their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:08.720
frequent customers. Oona has brought several guys&nbsp;
to the facility in hopes of finding her soulmate.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:13.200
Her boyfriend is clearly nervous before going&nbsp;
in because if their timer doesn’t match,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:17.280
they will have to break up.
Patty makes him sign a document and embeds his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:22.880
wrist with the implant. It starts to blink almost&nbsp;
immediately showing him that he has two years left&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:27.760
to meet his soulmate. Oona looks at her timer&nbsp;
hoping for it to start blinking but it never&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:32.800
does. Her boyfriend is glad that he will meet his&nbsp;
soulmate right when he finishes medical school.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:37.600
After finding out they are not the one for each&nbsp;
other, they break up and go their separate ways.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:43.040
Oona's stepsister and roommate, Steph, has a timer&nbsp;
that says she will not meet her soulmate for over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:48.480
15 years. Since she isn’t going to wait for that&nbsp;
long, Steph's lifestyle includes one-night stands&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:54.080
with men who are only looking for a fling like&nbsp;
her. One day, Oona is at a grocery store when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:59.360
the cashier named Mikey starts a conversation&nbsp;
with her. His compliments flatter Oona but she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:05.120
notices he already has a timer that has a specific&nbsp;
date on it, meaning that he is not her soulmate.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:09.840
Mikey also notices her timer but suggests they&nbsp;
can still see each other because soulmates are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:15.120
in the future anyway. At night, the sisters go&nbsp;
to their parents for dinner but Steph is late&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:20.320
as always. She notices Oona is sad about her&nbsp;
ex-boyfriend and advises her to resort to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:24.960
one night stands until she meets the one. 
At their parent’s house, everyone is excited&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:29.680
for their younger brother Jesse to get his&nbsp;
timer embedded for the first time. They have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:34.800
even invited a matchmaker to celebrate the event&nbsp;
together. The matchmaker plants the implant and it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:40.480
immediately shows Jess only has three days left&nbsp;
to meet his soulmate. Everyone is happy for him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:45.280
but Oona thinks it’s unfair. She congratulates&nbsp;
her little brother and leaves without waiting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:51.120
for dinner. She drives back to the grocery store&nbsp;
to meet Mikey. At first, she hesitates to go in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:56.480
but does it anyway. Mikey is left stunned when&nbsp;
she asks him out. He quickly asks his co-worker&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.480 --> 00:03:01.440
to take his place and follows her back to the&nbsp;
car. The car ride to Mikey’s home is awkward&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:06.240
as the two don’t have anything in common to talk&nbsp;
about. They finally reach Mikey’s apartment and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:11.840
are greeted by four of his roommates. The house&nbsp;
is trashed with beer bottles and tissue papers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:16.240
which makes Oona rethink her decision.&nbsp;
She also tells Mikey that she is turning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:20.880
thirty soon and regrets it instantly. 
When she is about to leave, Mikey persuades her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:26.560
to stay and the two finally kiss. But she notices&nbsp;
his timer again which only has four months left&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:32.240
in it. Oona realizes what she is doing is wrong&nbsp;
and leaves after apologizing. The following day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:37.280
she is surprised by Mikey coming to her job as&nbsp;
a patient. He assumes that she doesn’t like him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:45.280
because he is a cashier and explains that he&nbsp;
does music as well. He tries to persuade her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:50.800
claiming that the timer only shows you a definite&nbsp;
path and life is about detours. But Oona bluntly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:56.160
states that he is not the one for her so she is&nbsp;
not wasting time on him. Moreover, she feels like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.160 --> 00:04:01.680
he is cheating on his future soulmate. At night,&nbsp;
she goes on a blind date with a man but is clearly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:07.440
very bored. He only talks when she asks him&nbsp;
questions, so the date ends on a bad note. To get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:13.200
over it, Oona goes to a club and meets Mikey yet&nbsp;
again. He is a drummer in the band performing at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:19.120
the club. The two make eye contact and end up in&nbsp;
Mikey’s room at the end of the day. As they make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:24.400
out, his roommates arrive at the house and disturb&nbsp;
them. Mikey asks all of them to shut up because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:28.800
this is the only chance he will get with someone&nbsp;
like Oona who is way out of his league. 
&nbsp;

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:34.000
Meanwhile, Steph is at her job as a receptionist&nbsp;
at a nursing home when a handsome man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:39.840
named Dan walks in. She is interested in him but&nbsp;
is disappointed to notice he doesn’t have a timer.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:44.720
At home, she asks Oona about her night and is&nbsp;
proud of her for finally getting with a guy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:49.520
She also advises her to never meet him again&nbsp;
because she might get hurt. It is finally the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:55.360
day Oona’s brother gets to meet his soulmate. His&nbsp;
parents excitedly send him to school but the whole&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.360 --> 00:05:01.040
day passes without his timer ringing. When he&nbsp;
finally returns home, their house maid introduces&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.040 --> 00:05:06.800
him to her daughter Soledad and the timer finally&nbsp;
goes off. While Jesse's mother is excited,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:12.240
Soledad’s parents rudely leave the premises with&nbsp;
her. In the evening, Oona is about to return home&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:18.160
from work when Mikey startles her. She hits him in&nbsp;
the face but quickly composes herself, and the two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:24.240
drive back to her house. Oona kisses him after&nbsp;
making sure Steph isn’t around. Starting then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:28.960
they start to date. Oona goes to his house&nbsp;
frequently and makes friends with his roommates.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:33.440
She tells him about her biological father&nbsp;
who is a music producer. She hasn’t talked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.440 --> 00:05:38.880
to him since he and his mother broke up.
One day at work, Steph gets yelled at by her boss&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:44.960
for not receiving calls. Dan lies to him and gets&nbsp;
her out of the situation. He is clearly interested&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.960 --> 00:05:50.800
in Steph but she seems to not care. Still, she&nbsp;
asks him out, planning to set up a date between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:56.320
him and Oona. She tells Oona to be at the club in&nbsp;
the evening because she hasn’t been out lately.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.320 --> 00:06:02.400
Oona feels bad for not telling Steph about Mikey&nbsp;
but she is afraid of being judged. Later that day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:08.400
Steph and Dan wait for Oona at the bar for a long&nbsp;
time but she doesn’t come. Instead, she hangs out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:13.840
with Mikey in her room. Steph and Dan talk for&nbsp;
a long time. Dan tells her about his wife who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:19.280
died three years ago. He believes that she was his&nbsp;
soulmate so he never had to plant the timer on his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.280 --> 00:06:24.480
wrist. As the conversation continues, they start&nbsp;
to like each other. But when Steph returns home,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:30.080
she is furious at Oona for abandoning her. She&nbsp;
sees Mikey in her room and figures out they have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:34.560
been seeing each other in secret. Things get&nbsp;
heated when the sisters begin to argue about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:39.680
Mikey’s timer. He interrupts them and reveals that&nbsp;
his timer is actually a sticker that he bought so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.680 --> 00:06:44.560
he would feel included. He doesn’t actually&nbsp;
believe in timers and would never get one.
&nbsp;

00:06:44.560 --> 00:06:50.960
Oona is in utter shock and mad at him for lying&nbsp;
to her all along. She furiously asks him to leave.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.960 --> 00:06:55.200
Their time together had only been enjoyable&nbsp;
because she thought it wouldn’t last long,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:59.920
now that she knows he doesn’t have a timer, she&nbsp;
feels betrayed. For the next week, she doesn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.920 --> 00:07:05.440
try to contact him but is miserable at the same&nbsp;
time. She finally decides to talk to him and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.440 --> 00:07:10.640
tells him that she is sorry. They meet at Oona’s&nbsp;
parents’ house for thanksgiving. Their house maid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.640 --> 00:07:15.280
and her daughter have also gathered for the&nbsp;
meal. Mikey knows how to speak in Spanish so he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:20.400
gets along with them easily. Oona answers all the&nbsp;
questions that her parents ask Mikey and doesn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:26.160
let him speak. It is evident that she is ashamed&nbsp;
of being in a relationship with someone so young&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.160 --> 00:07:32.640
and naive. Meanwhile, Dan and Steph meet&nbsp;
a couple of times and start dating. Oona,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:38.080
on the other hand, is now unsure how she feels&nbsp;
about Mikey. Moreover, her mother urges her to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.080 --> 00:07:43.680
find out if Mikey is her soulmate as soon&nbsp;
as possible. One day, he suddenly confesses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:49.280
that he loves her but Oona panics and leaves. 
She and Steph then go to see Oona’s biological&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.280 --> 00:07:54.320
father Rick. They are received by a young&nbsp;
woman who happens to be Rick’s girlfriend.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:59.200
The first few minutes are awkward because Oona&nbsp;
hasn’t talked to him for a long time. Then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:05.040
she bluntly asks him why he never got a timer. The&nbsp;
man shows her the timer on his wrist and tells her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:10.880
he has one but he still has some time left to meet&nbsp;
his soulmate. Then, his girlfriend tells them she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:16.320
had her timer removed because she loves Rick and&nbsp;
doesn’t care what the timer says. The sisters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.320 --> 00:08:20.880
are inspired by her, so they rush to get theirs&nbsp;
removed, promising to live their life without&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.880 --> 00:08:26.480
depending on a stupid countdown. Matchmaker Kaite&nbsp;
is in utter shock to find out the girls want to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:31.920
remove their timers. She and the manager warn them&nbsp;
that if the device is removed once, they cannot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.920 --> 00:08:37.840
replant it again so this will be their last chance&nbsp;
of finding true love. Steph says she doesn’t care&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.840 --> 00:08:43.760
and finally removes hers. But when it is Oona’s&nbsp;
turn, she hesitates. Seconds before it is removed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.760 --> 00:08:49.360
the timer starts to beep. It turns out that her&nbsp;
soulmate got his timer embedded right then.
&nbsp;

00:08:49.360 --> 00:08:55.120
Oona only has five hours to meet him. She decides&nbsp;
to leave it on for that time out of curiosity but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.120 --> 00:09:01.680
Steph gets mad at her. The following day is their&nbsp;
shared birthday. At night, Oona’s countdown stops,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:06.560
meaning she will meet her soulmate the next&nbsp;
day. Their mother organizes a birthday party&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:12.800
for the two of them. She has invited Dan and Mikey&nbsp;
both. Steph arrives at the house first and hangs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.800 --> 00:09:17.840
out with Dan. Mikey, on the other hand, is busy&nbsp;
translating a conversation between the housemaid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:23.360
and Oona’s mother. They decide to stay as boss and&nbsp;
worker and let their kids take their relationship&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.360 --> 00:09:29.040
further themselves. When Oona arrives at the&nbsp;
party, her timer rings along with Dan’s, meaning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:35.200
that he is her soulmate. An annoyed Steph storms&nbsp;
off to the kitchen while Mikey leaves for his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:40.640
house. Dan follows Steph behind and asks her if&nbsp;
she is okay. Oona joins the two to talk about the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:46.160
situation. Steph starts to yell at Oona for always&nbsp;
getting everything she wants in life. She believes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:51.680
that Oona has taken away Dan, who is the only&nbsp;
person she was ever interested in. The sisters get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.680 --> 00:09:57.040
into a fight which ends when Oona tells Steph she&nbsp;
is her best friend and she doesn’t want Dan.
&nbsp;

00:09:57.600 --> 00:10:02.640
After Oona leaves, Dan tells Steph that he got a&nbsp;
timer because it was important for her and that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.640 --> 00:10:08.080
he doesn’t care for her sister. The following&nbsp;
morning, Oona goes to meet Mikey at his house.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:12.160
She shows him that she got her timer&nbsp;
removed because she wants to be with him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.160 --> 00:10:19.920
Mikey is confused at first but then finally kisses&nbsp;
her. The next day, Steph wakes Oona up and they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.920 --> 00:10:25.440
solve their differences. In the last scene,&nbsp;
Oona then goes out on a run and coincidentally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.440 --> 00:10:30.640
meets Dan. They talk for a while and find&nbsp;
out they have a lot in common. But at last,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:35.120
they laugh and go their separate ways. 
